    <item>
      <title>Democrats Need to Make Jobs Central to Economic Policy</title>
      <link>https://www.bloomberg.com/opinion/articles/2026-11-10/democrats-need-to-make-jobs-central-to-economic-policy</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">cab6f7a329c146b485046d9f</guid>
      <pubDate>Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:00:07 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>When it comes to the economy, newly elected Democrats have an intimidating to-do list. Voters were clear that they are struggling to afford their life, so the party needs to address deeply entrenched problems in markets for health insurance, housing, utilities, and elder and childcare. And in order to do any of that, Congress has to get the fiscal balance sheet in order and reform the tax code.</description>
      <dc:creator>Kathryn Anne Edwards</dc:creator>
